{"step_index":42,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T15:28:27Z","thinking":"**Drafting README.md**\n\nI'm now outlining the README.md file, focusing on providing comprehensive academic documentation for the StreamWave platform. I'm structuring it to cover an overview, architecture, and explain the Vercel serverless model. I'll include sections on the project structure, prerequisites, installation, and audio aspects.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"# StreamWave Serverless Media Platform\n\nAcademic prototype of a serverless media streaming application built for **StreamWave Entertainment** (a fictional Zimbabwean entertainment company). Constructed with **Python 3.12** and **FastAPI**, engineered specifically for deployment on **Vercel Functions**.\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Key Features & Architectural Highlights\n\n- **Vercel Serverless Native**: Designed without continuous background processes, SQLite, or runtime filesystem writes to respect Vercel's read-only/ephemeral execution model.\n- **FastAPI & Pydantic Validation**: Strict type annotations and schema validation for all requests and responses.\n- **Static Asset Streaming**: Non-copyrighted WAV audio generated via Python standard library and served directly as a static asset (`/media/demo.wav`).\n- **Structured Logged Playback Events**: `POST /api/play-events` validates media IDs, attaches UTC server timestamps, and emits structured JSON event logs directly to the Python logger without requiring database persistence.\n- **StreamWave Responsive UI**: Dark graphite styling (`#121214`), restrained red accent (`#e50914`), clean rectangular media cards, accessibility-focused HTML5 audio player, and `<dialog>` details modal.\n\n---\n\n## 📂 Project Structure\n\n```\n.\n├── app.py                      # FastAPI application entry point & static file routing\n├── data/\n│   └── media.json              # Read-only Zimbabwean media catalogue\n├── public/\n│   ├── css/\n│   │   └── styles.css          # Dark graphite responsive CSS design\n│   ├── js/\n│   │   └── app.js              # Vanilla JavaScript frontend logic & API client\n│   ├── media/\n│   │   └── demo.wav            # Generated demonstration WAV audio asset\n│   └── index.html              # StreamWave HTML5 web interface\n├── scripts/\n│   └── generate_demo_audio.py  # Python stdlib script generating synthesized WAV chime\n├── tests/\n│   └── test_api.py             # Pytest automated test suite covering all API routes\n├── pyproject.toml              # Python 3.12 environment & tool configurations\n├── requirements.txt            # Pinned dependencies (FastAPI, Uvicorn, Pydantic, Pytest, HTTPX)\n├── .gitignore                  # Source control ignore configuration\n└── README.md                   # Technical documentation\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🛠️ Installation & Local Setup\n\n### 1. Prerequisites\n- Python **3.12+** installed on your system.\n\n### 2. Clone / Navigate to Project Directory\n```bash\ncd streamwave-serverless\n```\n\n### 3. Create Virtual Environment & Install Dependencies\n```bash\npython -m venv .venv\n# On Windows:\n.venv\\Scripts\\activate\n# On Linux/macOS:\nsource .venv/bin/activate\n\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n### 4. Generate Demonstration Audio Asset\nRun the pure Python standard library generator to synthesize `public/media/demo.wav`:\n```bash\npython scripts/generate_demo_audio.py\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🧪 Running Automated Tests\n\nRun `pytest` to execute the automated test suite covering health, media catalogue, search/filtering, detail lookups, 404 handling, and play event logging:\n\n```bash\npytest tests/test_api.py -v\n```\n\n---\n\n## 💻 Running the Application Locally\n\nLaunch the Uvicorn development server:\n\n```bash\nuvicorn app:app --reload --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000\n```\n\nOnce running:\n- **Web Interface**: Open [http://127.0.0.1:8000](http://127.0.0.1:8000) in your browser.\n- **Interactive OpenAPI / Swagger Documentation**: Open [http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs](http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs).\n- **ReDoc Documentation**: Open [http://127.0.0.1:8000/redoc](http://127.0.0.1:8000/redoc).\n\n---\n\n## 📡 API Endpoints Reference\n\n| Method | Endpoint | Query / Body Params | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `GET` | `/api/health` | None | Returns health status, platform info, and ISO 8601 server timestamp. |\n| `GET` | `/api/media` | `query`, `type`, `genre` | Retrieves media items with optional search query and type/genre filters. |\n| `GET` | `/api/media/{media_id}` | `media_id` (path) | Retrieves single media item by ID or returns HTTP 404 if not found. |\n| `POST` | `/api/play-events` | `media_id`, `session_id`, `client_timestamp` | Validates media ID, attaches server timestamp, and logs event to standard output. |\n\n---\n\n## ☁️ Deployment to Vercel\n\nThis application conforms to the official Vercel FastAPI deployment standard:\n1. `app.py` exposes `app = FastAPI(...)`.\n2. Static assets in `public/` are served natively by Vercel's edge network or mounted via `app.mount(\"/\", StaticFiles(...))` for unified fallback.\n3. Deploy to Vercel using the Vercel CLI:\n   ```bash\n   vercel\n   ```\n","Description":"Create README.md with setup instructions and API docs","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\dell\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\\README.md","toolAction":"Creating README.md","toolSummary":"Creating README.md"}}]}
